('advanced-native-1282', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1282-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["Giving callers enough space to explain what they need."],"options":["Judging the programme only by how polished its introduction sounds.","Replacing callers’ questions with the host’s prepared examples.","Giving callers enough space to explain what they need.","Keeping every call as short as possible to preserve the opening sequence."]},"advanced-native-1282-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The host needs to understand the actual question before responding to it.","A smooth introduction cannot substitute for hearing what someone needs.","If callers are cut off, the programme loses the information its advice depends on.","The programme lives or dies by people being able to explain their questions."],"options":["The host needs to understand the actual question before responding to it.","A smooth introduction cannot substitute for hearing what someone needs.","If callers are cut off, the programme loses the information its advice depends on.","The programme lives or dies by people being able to explain their questions."]},"advanced-native-1282-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["For this purpose, the newsletter lives or dies by reaching readers before they need to act."],"options":["Sending the newsletter late shows that its translations must also be inaccurate.","For this purpose, the newsletter lives or dies by reaching readers before they need to act.","Because the translation is accurate, the arrival date cannot affect the newsletter’s purpose."]},"advanced-native-1282-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["強調一項對成敗十分關鍵的依賴。"],"options":["強調一項對成敗十分關鍵的依賴。","表示某人將因指定原因真的死亡。","只是在列出一個無關緊要的小偏好。"]},"advanced-native-1282-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["The programme lives or dies by hearing the questions, so a microphone check supports that aim rather than competing with it."],"options":["We should keep the opening polished even if callers cannot be heard clearly.","We should replace open questions with the host’s prepared script so callers cannot slow the programme.","The programme lives or dies by hearing the questions, so a microphone check supports that aim rather than competing with it."]},"advanced-native-1282-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["The tour lives or dies by having someone who knows the route, and I can cover only two sessions. Let us confirm the other guides before publishing ten time slots.","These walks live or die by reliable guiding, so we should not offer dates on other volunteers’ behalf. Could we list only the two sessions I can lead and add more when other guides agree?"],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1283', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1283-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["The quote showed high costs, while the visit supplied evidence about the welcome."],"options":["The visit showed that the manager had refused to discuss the group’s needs.","The quote showed high costs, while the visit supplied evidence about the welcome.","The warm welcome confirmed that the written charges were lower than expected.","The written quote covered the room alone, while meal prices would be discussed at the visit."]},"advanced-native-1283-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["It looked expensive on paper because both the room and meal charges were high.","The quoted figures already showed substantial charges for the two main items.","I was judging the written costs, before we had experienced the welcome.","The price information gave me a cost judgement, even though the visit could tell me something different about the place."],"options":["It looked expensive on paper because both the room and meal charges were high.","The quoted figures already showed substantial charges for the two main items.","I was judging the written costs, before we had experienced the welcome.","The price information gave me a cost judgement, even though the visit could tell me something different about the place."]},"advanced-native-1283-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Expensive on paper refers to the written cost information here, not evidence that the performance is impressive."],"options":["Expensive on paper refers to the written cost information here, not evidence that the performance is impressive.","The phrase says that the audience has already praised the performance.","The phrase means that the theatre has agreed to reduce the rent."]},"advanced-native-1283-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["所有親身體驗過的人都認為它物有所值。"],"options":["實際體驗可以提供價格以外的資料。","書面資料讓人覺得費用高。","所有親身體驗過的人都認為它物有所值。"]},"advanced-native-1283-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["It is still expensive on paper; we can describe the welcome warmly without changing what the quote says."],"options":["I would describe the charges as high and assume the manager was unhelpful as well.","It is still expensive on paper; we can describe the welcome warmly without changing what the quote says.","I would call the quote cheap because the welcome made me feel comfortable."]},"advanced-native-1283-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["This camp looks expensive on paper, but the fee sheet does not tell us what the lessons involve. I can record the cost and ask for the programme before we compare the teaching.","I would mark it as expensive on paper rather than label it the best camp. Could we add a column for the programme details we still need, so the table shows the limits of our information?"],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1284', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1284-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["Invited family stories to help people join the conversation."],"options":["Invited family stories to help people join the conversation.","Removed the family-story slot to leave more time for formal speeches.","Asked new partners to wait outside until the decoration work was finished.","Left the introductions to the venue staff instead of inviting family contributions."]},"advanced-native-1284-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["We wanted the welcome to involve what people could share, not only what we could hire.","Money can buy the setting, but we still needed something that helped people talk together.","A comfortable venue did not by itself give newcomers a place in the conversation.","The stories gave families a shared activity rather than just a room to sit in."],"options":["We wanted the welcome to involve what people could share, not only what we could hire.","Money can buy the setting, but we still needed something that helped people talk together.","A comfortable venue did not by itself give newcomers a place in the conversation.","The stories gave families a shared activity rather than just a room to sit in."]},"advanced-native-1284-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Money can buy the setting, and this host has also made specific arrangements for the people attending."],"options":["Paying for a quiet room shows that the host has left the guests’ needs to the venue alone.","The host has checked dietary needs but has left no place for the new colleague at the meal.","Money can buy the setting, and this host has also made specific arrangements for the people attending."]},"advanced-native-1284-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["只要付費租場，主人就必定不在意賓客。"],"options":["只要付費租場，主人就必定不在意賓客。","有合適場地，也仍可需要介紹及參與安排。","場地安排與人際互動需要分別考慮。"]},"advanced-native-1284-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["Money can buy the setting; we should choose a useful one and plan how people will join in, rather than drop either task."],"options":["Then we should spend the whole planning meeting on decorations before discussing who is coming.","We can assume people will find somewhere to sit once they have a story to tell.","Money can buy the setting; we should choose a useful one and plan how people will join in, rather than drop either task."]},"advanced-native-1284-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Money can buy the setting, but a larger stage will not give her the conversations she has asked for. Could we keep a comfortable room and shorten the programme so she can speak with everyone?","Money can buy the setting; it cannot replace listening to the person we are celebrating. Let us use the room for short conversations rather than add a performance she does not want."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1287', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1287-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["The tickets were affordable, but the journey home still needed a workable arrangement."],"options":["The speaker asked for a later performance to catch the last train before the encore.","The tickets were affordable, but the journey home still needed a workable arrangement.","The speaker had rejected the concert solely because the tickets cost too much.","The affordable ticket already included a guaranteed train after the encore."]},"advanced-native-1287-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The tickets would not break the bank; getting home was the difficulty I still needed to solve.","I could manage the ticket price, but the last train did not suit the original finish time.","An earlier performance might let me enjoy the concert without missing the train.","The cost was acceptable to me; the timetable was the part that needed checking."],"options":["The tickets would not break the bank; getting home was the difficulty I still needed to solve.","I could manage the ticket price, but the last train did not suit the original finish time.","An earlier performance might let me enjoy the concert without missing the train.","The cost was acceptable to me; the timetable was the part that needed checking."]},"advanced-native-1287-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Saying it would break the bank expresses that it costs more than she is prepared to spend here, not proof of actual bankruptcy."],"options":["The phrase establishes that she has already bought the coat and cannot pay her rent.","Choosing not to buy it means she thinks the coat has no value to anyone.","Saying it would break the bank expresses that it costs more than she is prepared to spend here, not proof of actual bankruptcy."]},"advanced-native-1287-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["每位參加者都願意支付完全相同的金額。"],"options":["每位參加者都願意支付完全相同的金額。","說話者想找費用可接受的慶祝方式。","慶祝不一定要超出能接受的花費。"]},"advanced-native-1287-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["It will not break the bank, but I still need a way home; could we check the earlier performance?"],"options":["I would tell everyone the tickets are too expensive rather than explain the train problem.","It will not break the bank, but I still need a way home; could we check the earlier performance?","The affordable price is enough for me to treat the whole evening, including the journey home, as arranged."]},"advanced-native-1287-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Let us choose a gift that will not break the bank for the people contributing, rather than order first and divide the bill afterwards. I can help with the photographs, and we could ask privately what each person is comfortable offering.","I would like to help make the album without breaking the bank, so I can offer time and a small voluntary contribution. Could we check people’s wishes before choosing the edition, without asking anyone to justify their budget?"],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1290', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1290-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["They enjoyed some parts privately and greeted others without joining the crowded games."],"options":["They joined the games all evening and asked for louder group activities.","They avoided the gate because they did not want anyone to know they had moved in.","They disliked the lights and asked the organisers to remove them.","They enjoyed some parts privately and greeted others without joining the crowded games."]},"advanced-native-1290-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["Their own account matched the private walk they chose after dinner.","They liked the lights but did not want the same group activities as everyone else.","They mostly kept to themselves and chose a quiet walk instead of the crowded games.","They told us they preferred not to join the busiest activities."],"options":["Their own account matched the private walk they chose after dinner.","They liked the lights but did not want the same group activities as everyone else.","They mostly kept to themselves and chose a quiet walk instead of the crowded games.","They told us they preferred not to join the busiest activities."]},"advanced-native-1290-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["She did not share that information; this does not say she kept to herself socially."],"options":["She did not share that information; this does not say she kept to herself socially.","She spent the evening alone and avoided all conversation.","She announced the move but refused to discuss why it was happening."]},"advanced-native-1290-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["他們一定不喜歡住在附近的人。"],"options":["他們一定不喜歡住在附近的人。","更多情境可以說明他們是否偏好私人空間。","他們不太與別人交往。"]},"advanced-native-1290-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["They may keep to themselves without wanting us to ignore them; we can greet them and let them choose how much to join."],"options":["They may keep to themselves without wanting us to ignore them; we can greet them and let them choose how much to join.","We should treat the quiet walk as a request to be removed from every future invitation.","I would put their names into the next crowded game to help them stop being private."]},"advanced-native-1290-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["I was wrong to call her unfriendly just because she keeps to herself. After speaking with her, I understand that she welcomes a brief chat, and I should not have guessed her feelings from her attendance.","Keeping to herself does not mean she wants no contact, and I withdraw my earlier description. We can offer a greeting without sharing her private reasons or promising that she will attend the next event."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1291', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1291-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["Singing connected the family gathering with two neighbours, not every resident."],"options":["Singing connected the family gathering with two neighbours, not every resident.","Every upstairs resident stopped their evening and came down to sing.","The gathering began in the courtyard and then moved entirely indoors.","The neighbours asked the relatives to stop before hearing any song."]},"advanced-native-1291-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["Part of the shared evening grew from a gathering inside one home.","The celebration spilled out of the home as the singing reached the courtyard and two neighbours joined.","The open doorway let the family’s singing connect with people outside.","Two neighbours took part in a chorus that had begun with the relatives."],"options":["Part of the shared evening grew from a gathering inside one home.","The celebration spilled out of the home as the singing reached the courtyard and two neighbours joined.","The open doorway let the family’s singing connect with people outside.","Two neighbours took part in a chorus that had begun with the relatives."]},"advanced-native-1291-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The account does not show a celebration spilling out of the home; the music travels from the street towards the room."],"options":["The account describes the readers leaving home to lead the parade.","The account does not show a celebration spilling out of the home; the music travels from the street towards the room.","The account describes the household’s singing reaching the parade outside."]},"advanced-native-1291-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["整條街每個人都感到同樣快樂。"],"options":["可以補充它延伸到哪個公共地方。","整條街每個人都感到同樣快樂。","氣氛被描述為由私人空間向外延伸。"]},"advanced-native-1291-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["The celebration spilled out of the home, but we saw two neighbours join, not every household."],"options":["I would describe it as an indoor-only event because some residents stayed upstairs.","The celebration spilled out of the home, but we saw two neighbours join, not every household.","I would count the upstairs residents as participants because they lived near the courtyard."]},"advanced-native-1291-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["It is lovely to see the celebration spilling out of the home, but these chairs are blocking the path for my pushchair. Could we move them to one side so you can keep celebrating and everyone can get through?","Your birthday gathering has spilled out of the home and made the courtyard lively. Could you leave a clear route to the entrance so I can bring the pushchair home without interrupting the gathering?"],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1293', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1293-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["Possible meeting places, while people and times still needed agreement."],"options":["A list of people who had confirmed the same time at each venue.","Instructions that required all friends to join relatives at one table.","Possible meeting places, while people and times still needed agreement.","Three meetings that every family had already agreed to attend."]},"advanced-native-1293-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["Groups could use the suggestions when deciding where to meet.","We wanted to show possible spaces before people agreed their own times.","A quiet meeting place could be useful even though the actual guests were not yet confirmed.","They offered places to gather with family or friends without fixing anyone’s plans for them."],"options":["Groups could use the suggestions when deciding where to meet.","We wanted to show possible spaces before people agreed their own times.","A quiet meeting place could be useful even though the actual guests were not yet confirmed.","They offered places to gather with family or friends without fixing anyone’s plans for them."]},"advanced-native-1293-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["People can gather with family or friends here; the wording offers a choice rather than requiring both groups."],"options":["Choosing friends means the organiser has refused to welcome relatives.","People can gather with family or friends here; the wording offers a choice rather than requiring both groups.","The wording requires each guest to bring one relative and one friend."]},"advanced-native-1293-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["每位參加者都必定與主人有親屬關係。"],"options":["可以再交代相聚的時間、地方及原因。","他們與親屬或朋友相聚。","每位參加者都必定與主人有親屬關係。"]},"advanced-native-1293-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["The map suggests places to gather with family or friends; we should ask about people and times before confirming a meeting."],"options":["Let us assign every grou